    text:"Pennsylvania Governor Josh Shapiro signed Executive Order 2026-05, requiring state agencies to only evaluate data-center permit applications from developers who make a legally binding commitment to GRID Requirements (energy affordability, environmental protection, workforce standards, transparency, local approval) — and removed all AI data-center projects from the state's Permit Fast Track Program. Shapiro's office says over 100 data-center proposals are under discussion in the state, most speculative and lacking financing or tenant agreements.",
