    text:"Unitree Robotics, a Hangzhou-based humanoid robot maker, surged 460% in its Shanghai stock market debut on August 19, raising 6.1 billion yuan ($904 million) in the IPO. The company became the world's first listed humanoid-robot maker in mainland China, with backers including DeepSeek (which invested 140.8 million yuan) and prior investor Tencent. Unitree's latest model, 'Superman,' can jump 2 meters and run at speeds up to 12.66 meters per second.",
